WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:14.367
Molly and her mother were shopping for clothes on a Saturday afternoon,

2
00:00:14.368 --> 00:00:21.592
but every time Molly found something she liked, her mother said, "That's too expensive, Molly."

3
00:00:21.593 --> 00:00:25.507
In the end, Molly's mother chose an ugly pair of pants.

4
00:00:25.508 --> 00:00:29.561
"I'm never going to wear them!" Molly complained.

5
00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:34.836
Molly's mother was very careful about spending money.

6
00:00:34.837 --> 00:00:39.109
"Money doesn't grow on trees," she always said.

7
00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:46.236
"Oh, hi, Molly!" It was Molly's friend Erica, who was shopping with her mother in the same store.

8
00:00:46.237 --> 00:00:49.519
"Hi, Erica!" Molly said.

9
00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:55.251
"Things are so expensive these days, aren't they?" said Erica's mom.

10
00:00:55.252 --> 00:01:00.789
"Yes, I can't believe the prices!" agreed Molly's mother.

11
00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:09.424
"Mom, I want that!" said Erica, pointing to an expensive face cleanser.

12
00:01:09.425 --> 00:01:14.889
"Of course, honey. One? Two? No, let's take three."

13
00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:18.543
Erica's mother put some bottles into her shopping cart.

14
00:01:18.544 --> 00:01:21.995
"Well, we should get going. Good-bye!"

15
00:01:21.996 --> 00:01:26.562
"Mom? Can I have some too?" asked Molly.

16
00:01:26.563 --> 00:01:34.445
"Honey, this is really overpriced," Molly's mother answered, "but if you want, we can get one."

17
00:01:34.446 --> 00:01:41.242
"No, I want more," Molly said.

18
00:01:41.243 --> 00:01:45.654
"One is more than enough," her mother said firmly.

19
00:01:45.655 --> 00:01:50.678
Molly's family wasn't poor, but her parents didn't buy Molly whatever she wanted.

20
00:01:50.679 --> 00:01:54.460
"Money isn't everything," her father would say.

21
00:01:54.461 --> 00:01:58.310
"The real valuable things in life cannot be bought with money."

22
00:01:58.311 --> 00:02:04.681
"And money doesn't grow on trees," her mother would add.

23
00:02:04.682 --> 00:02:09.507
The next day, Molly and her friends were looking at magazines at Jenny's house.

24
00:02:09.508 --> 00:02:17.004
"Wow! I'm going to ask my mom to buy me this!" Esther exclaimed, pointing to the dress in a fashion ad.

25
00:02:17.005 --> 00:02:24.090
"Oh, this is so nice! I'll tell my dad I want this for my birthday!" Sharon said.

26
00:02:24.091 --> 00:02:28.713
"See what I got?" Jenny held up a pretty blue shirt.

27
00:02:28.714 --> 00:02:35.416
"It's so cute! How much was it?" asked Sharon.

28
00:02:35.417 --> 00:02:39.417
"I don't know, but it has a matching hat. See?"

29
00:02:39.418 --> 00:02:42.419
Molly felt so jealous of her friends.

30
00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:47.882
"Why are my parents so stingy with money?" she thought to herself.

31
00:02:47.883 --> 00:02:51.511
As she was walking home, something on the sidewalk caught her eye.

32
00:02:51.512 --> 00:02:55.009
Molly bent down to pick it up. It was a purse.

33
00:02:55.010 --> 00:03:01.399
"Someone must have dropped it!" she said, looking for the owner.

34
00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:05.072
There was no one around, so Molly opened the purse.

35
00:03:05.073 --> 00:03:08.813
She gasped! The purse was filled with cash!

36
00:03:08.814 --> 00:03:13.393
"Oh no! What should I do?" Molly wondered.

37
00:03:13.394 --> 00:03:19.208
"I should take it to the police station, but what if the owner never comes to claim it?

38
00:03:19.209 --> 00:03:27.981
Maybe I could take just a little bit of money and then take it to the police station?"

39
00:03:27.982 --> 00:03:33.138
At home, Molly did not tell her parents about the purse and went upstairs to bed.

40
00:03:33.139 --> 00:03:40.233
As she thought about keeping the money, a strange feeling stirred inside of her, something she had never felt before.

41
00:03:40.234 --> 00:03:43.447
Two voices began to argue in her head.

42
00:03:43.448 --> 00:03:46.862
"Take the money," said Molly the Red.

43
00:03:46.863 --> 00:03:54.740
"No! Turn it in to the police!" said Molly the White.

44
00:03:54.741 --> 00:03:58.525
"No one will know if you take it!" said the Red.

45
00:03:58.526 --> 00:04:03.288
"It's not yours. You can't keep it!" said the White.

46
00:04:03.289 --> 00:04:10.476
Molly wasn't sure which voice to listen to, but when she thought of all the things she could buy, she decided to take the money.

47
00:04:10.477 --> 00:04:15.562
"Now you can buy anything you want!" said Molly the Red.

48
00:04:15.563 --> 00:04:21.370
"No, Molly! Don't do it!" Molly the White begged.

49
00:04:21.371 --> 00:04:24.623
Molly felt that strange feeling grow stronger.

50
00:04:24.624 --> 00:04:30.004
"Now you can be like your friends!" the Red whispered excitedly.

51
00:04:30.005 --> 00:04:33.987
Molly smiled and ignored the strange feeling inside.

52
00:04:33.988 --> 00:04:37.901
At the store, she realized it felt powerful to have so much money.

53
00:04:37.902 --> 00:04:44.503
"I'll take these two, please," she said, handing two pairs of shoes to the sales clerk.

54
00:04:44.504 --> 00:04:50.922
"Here you go," smiled the clerk. "Thank you and come again!"

55
00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:56.214
Molly also bought a new shirt and jeans, and decided to wear them on her way home.

56
00:04:56.215 --> 00:04:59.738
As she left the store, she bumped into her friends.

57
00:04:59.739 --> 00:05:04.483
"Molly! You look so stylish!" admired Erica.

58
00:05:04.484 --> 00:05:08.092
"Are those new jeans?" asked Jenny.

59
00:05:08.093 --> 00:05:12.378
"I love that shirt!" exclaimed Sharon.

60
00:05:12.379 --> 00:05:20.337
"Where did you get the money to buy these things?" Jenny asked.

61
00:05:20.338 --> 00:05:26.057
"I . . . my mom . . . gave . . . money . . ." Molly stammered.

62
00:05:26.058 --> 00:05:29.619
"It's none of your business!" she burst out.

63
00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:35.710
After she spent the rest of the day buying whatever she wanted, Molly took her purchases up to her bedroom.

64
00:05:35.711 --> 00:05:38.577
That strange feeling nudged at her heart again.

65
00:05:38.578 --> 00:05:44.353
"What is this I'm feeling?" she wondered. It was really bothering her.

66
00:05:44.354 --> 00:05:50.348
"I bought everything I wanted, so why am I not happy?"

67
00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:53.873
Molly picked up the empty purse and opened it up again.

68
00:05:53.874 --> 00:06:01.814
Inside was a letter. "Dear Mommy," the letter began, "I wish Daddy would recover soon.

69
00:06:01.815 --> 00:06:06.283
I don't have a lot, but here is some money I saved from working.

70
00:06:06.284 --> 00:06:09.426
Please use it for Daddy's hospital bills.

71
00:06:09.427 --> 00:06:12.919
I just want Daddy to be well again."

72
00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:16.617
As Molly read the letter, her eyes welled up with tears.

73
00:06:16.618 --> 00:06:23.745
"What have I done? What have I done?" she cried aloud. Her heart was aching.

74
00:06:23.746 --> 00:06:28.829
"What kind of person am I? I'm a thief!" she moaned.

75
00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:32.531
"I hate myself! I hate myself!"

76
00:06:32.532 --> 00:06:38.308
"Molly! Molly! Wake up, honey!" Molly's mother gently shook her.

77
00:06:38.309 --> 00:06:44.638
Molly was in her room, but the shopping bags and new shoes were gone.

78
00:06:44.639 --> 00:06:48.523
"You were having a nightmare," her mother said.

79
00:06:48.524 --> 00:06:51.051
Molly felt something against her back.

80
00:06:51.052 --> 00:06:55.778
It was the purse, and the money was still inside. Molly was relieved.

81
00:06:55.779 --> 00:07:00.555
She explained how she had found the purse, and confessed that she had wanted to keep the money.

82
00:07:00.556 --> 00:07:04.965
"I'm glad it was just a bad dream," Molly said.

83
00:07:04.966 --> 00:07:11.597
"Me too, honey, and I'm proud of you," her mother said.

84
00:07:11.598 --> 00:07:17.034
"How can you be proud of me? I wanted to keep the money!" Molly said.

85
00:07:17.035 --> 00:07:23.121
"But you didn't. You know that strange feeling you had?" her mother asked.

86
00:07:23.122 --> 00:07:28.617
"That was your conscience. It was telling you to do what was right.

87
00:07:28.618 --> 00:07:37.462
In the end, you listened to your conscience, your heart, and that's what's most important."

88
00:07:37.463 --> 00:07:44.473
"Mom, I learned that having the things I want doesn't make me happy," Molly said.

89
00:07:44.474 --> 00:07:47.519
"Money can't buy me happiness."

90
00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:49.287
"You're a good girl.

91
00:07:49.288 --> 00:07:57.329
It's good deeds that make a good heart," her mother said lovingly.
